body:
Three lists have to stay hand-synced here: the typed `Selector*` consts, this
map, and `AllSelectors()`. `TestAllSelectorsComplete` proves the map and the
slice agree, but nothing checks a newly-added const actually made it into
either — it would just silently never validate. Deriving the map from the
slice removes one of the three copies; the codebase already has precedent for
a small generic helper like this (see `addRule[T InstRule]` in base.go:165).

```suggestion
var selectors = toSet(AllSelectors())

// toSet builds a lookup set from an ordered slice, so the set can never
// drift from the slice it is derived from.
func toSet[T comparable](items []T) map[T]struct{} {
	set := make(map[T]struct{}, len(items))
	for _, item := range items {
		set[item] = struct{}{}
	}
	return set
}
```

